## The question S-F28 asks: does turning the four switches ON change the rate?

| comparison | rate OFF | rate ON | difference | verdict |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| bestmove asymmetry | 28.9 % | 34.3 % | +5.4 points | **consistent with 'the switches do not cause it'** |
| score asymmetry | 94.3 % | 94.6 % | +0.3 points | — |

Sample: 60 pairs per config, not their 353 — this checks the LEVEL of the rate and the OFF-vs-ON difference,not a reproduction of their exact counts. With 60 pairs the 95 % interval on a ~30 % rate is about +/-12 points,
so only a difference larger than that would contradict them.
